&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191047/rss" title="transitions.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Transitions.dev: Essential UI Transitions for Web Apps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The home page shows a series of cards, each of which displays a CSS-based UI animation. You can also install the set as an agent skill for your AI coding tool. Some of the transitions are part of a "Pro" plan. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191048/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Source code&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jakub Antalik &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191049/rss" title="markuplint.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Markuplint 5.0: An HTML Linter for All Markup Developers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — This well-established linter recently hit version 5. The &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191050/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;repo is here&lt;/a&gt;, and you can see things in action &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191051/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;in the playground&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yusuke Hirao &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191052/rss" title="www.soverybright.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Make Your Logo &lt;em&gt;Brighter&lt;/em&gt; Than White&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — If you've got an HDR display, this browser-based tool will quickly make its trick clear. Drop in your logo, choose which colors should glow, and get an HDR version ready to download. Claims to make things up to 7.5x brighter in Chrome and Safari.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chris Bennett &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🔊&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191053/rss" title="www.soundcn.xyz" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;soundcn: A Curated Collection of Sound Effects for Modern Web Apps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A comprehensive set of 800+ sounds that's installable via the shadcn registry. You can browse them by category and test each one by hovering over its card. Pay attention to the licenses of sounds you use. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191054/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;GitHub repo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kapish Dima &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
