&lt;p&gt;Here's a &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191057/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;kinda crude font foundry&lt;/a&gt; that takes two web fonts and mixes their glyphs, with &lt;em&gt;unsettling&lt;/em&gt; results. I mean, why not make a Times New Roman/Comic Sans hybrid to catch folks off guard? And, yes, you can download the end result.&lt;/p&gt;
